      "data_quality_notes": "Prior-year reserve movement: the primary movement note states a release of GBP 35.2m of \"technical reserves\" for prior periods (page 19). The note wording references technical reserves (which can include UPR as well as claims), and does not explicitly state whether this GBP 35.2m is a GROSS claims-outstanding movement or a NET figure after reinsurance. A gross claims development triangle is present in the report but is affected by a Reinsurance to Close (RITC) transaction of the UK Division shown in the Technical Reserves table (RITC of the UK Division (199.7) under claims outstanding) which distorts direct extraction of a reliable gross prior-year movement from the triangle. Given these ambiguities, the report-level narrative figure of a GBP 35.2m release has been used as the prior-year development (assumed to indicate an overall release); this has been flagged with moderate confidence. Lob-level movements are described qualitatively (predominantly Treaty, Energy and Marine) but not quantified in gross terms. The claims development triangle is present but was not used to compute prior-year movement due to RITC distortion and readibility limits in the scan. [RAG OVERRIDE: Model said PYD=-35.2, RAG triangle computed -134.0. Using RAG value.]",
